language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ N-puzzle: trace a sliding-tile puzzle from its start state to its end state in exactly N_STEPS states, each step moving the blank tile to an adjacent square, with no freezing.
given N_STEPS : int(1..)
given puzzle_start_dim1, puzzle_start_dim2 : int(1..)
given puzzle_start : matrix indexed by [int(1..puzzle_start_dim1), int(1..puzzle_start_dim2)] of int(0..)
given puzzle_end : matrix indexed by [int(1..puzzle_start_dim1), int(1..puzzle_start_dim2)] of int(0..)

$ steps[t,r,c] is the tile at row r, column c in state t (0 is the blank)
find steps : matrix indexed by [int(1..N_STEPS), int(1..puzzle_start_dim1), int(1..puzzle_start_dim2)] of int(0..puzzle_start_dim1*puzzle_start_dim2-1)
$ auxiliary: row and column of the blank tile in each state
find br : matrix indexed by [int(1..N_STEPS)] of int(1..puzzle_start_dim1)
find bc : matrix indexed by [int(1..N_STEPS)] of int(1..puzzle_start_dim2)

branching on [br, bc, steps]
such that
$ the first state is the start state of the puzzle
forAll r : int(1..puzzle_start_dim1) . forAll c : int(1..puzzle_start_dim2) . (steps[1,r,c] = puzzle_start[r,c]),
$ the last state is the end state of the puzzle
forAll r : int(1..puzzle_start_dim1) . forAll c : int(1..puzzle_start_dim2) . (steps[N_STEPS,r,c] = puzzle_end[r,c]),
$ each state holds every tile exactly once, the blank included
forAll t : int(1..N_STEPS) . allDiff([steps[t,r,c] | r : int(1..puzzle_start_dim1), c : int(1..puzzle_start_dim2)]),
$ the blank is at the position recorded for each state
forAll t : int(1..N_STEPS) . (steps[t,br[t],bc[t]] = 0),
$ each step moves the blank to an adjacent square (no freezing: the blank always moves)
forAll t : int(1..N_STEPS-1) . ((|br[t+1]-br[t]| + |bc[t+1]-bc[t]|) = 1),
$ the tile on the square the blank moves to slides into the old blank square
forAll t : int(1..N_STEPS-1) . forAll r : int(1..puzzle_start_dim1) . forAll c : int(1..puzzle_start_dim2) . ((br[t] = r /\ bc[t] = c) -> (steps[t+1,r,c] = steps[t,br[t+1],bc[t+1]])),
$ every other square keeps its tile from one state to the next
forAll t : int(1..N_STEPS-1) . forAll r : int(1..puzzle_start_dim1) . forAll c : int(1..puzzle_start_dim2) . (((br[t] != r \/ bc[t] != c) /\ (br[t+1] != r \/ bc[t+1] != c)) -> (steps[t+1,r,c] = steps[t,r,c]))
